today the issue becomes complicated  chechnya or chechen republic has  recalled the most important geopolitical  problem for the soviet union first and  then for the russian federation we find  ourselves here in a territory located on  the northern flank of the great caucasus  mostly flat and not very rich in natural  resources bordering georgia to the south  and three other autonomous republics of  the russian federation to the west  within gushetia and north of sesia to  the east with dagestan and to the  northwest with the russian cry of  stavropol it's not easy to establish the  productive potential of chechnya which  has been almost wiped out by the  destruction of war as far as industrial  plants are concerned and seriously  weakened in the agricultural sector as  well the main resource is the transit of  the oil pipeline linking the dagestan  city of mahatkara and the city of baku  in azerbaijan on the western shore of  the caspian sea with novarosis on the  black sea today's video is not intended  to be a detailed reconstruction of the  contrasts i would say almost secular  between this rebellious republic and  moscow because my friend simone has  already talked enough about it my intent  is rather to talk about the rise of its  current leader ramzan kadyrov because  even if officially chechnya today  presents a facade of peace and  reconstruction after the two conflicts  that have opposed it to the suffocating  grip of neighboring russia the tyranny  of its ruler established with the silent  blessing of the kremlin continues to  eradicate even the mildest forms of  descent through the law enforcement and  security agencies under his control  ramzan has used brutal methods of  repression abductions enforced  disappearances torture extrajudicial  executions and collective punishment  practices not only against the suspected  armed insurgents and their suspected  collaborators but also against other  action groups deemed inconvenient such  as independent journalists salafist  muslims drug users and those called  drunk driving let's take a few steps  back at the dawn of the third millennium  after larger scale russian military  operations had brought the chechnya back  under federal rule the kremlin gradually  began to hand over responsibility for  governing the republic and conducting  counter-insurgency operations to  pro-russian chechen leaders in his 2000  speech to the federal assembly putin  portrayed the chechnya as the supreme  obstacle to be overcome to hold the  country together saying russia has  received the fundamental challenge to  its sovereignty and territorial  integrity it has come face to face with  a force striving to redraw the  geopolitical map of the world the  domination of chechnya would have been  the cornerstone of putin's project of  building a strong state because it was  the emblem of the kremlin's control over  its subordinates putin's administration  through collaboration with the kadyrov  family set up the so-called policy of  chechenization that is changing the  nature of the conflict from russians  against the chechens to good chechens  against the rebel chechens and it's  likely that the russian president in  order to reinforce his statist vision  and end the ongoing conflict needed to  find the local lord with whom the local  population could identify and who knew  the intricate traditions of the country  it was necessary to appoint as president  someone who had the past in the ranks of  the insurrectionists and therefore enjoy  the good popular support ahmad  khadirov's past seemed a guarantee in  every aspect he was a sufi muslim who  didn't identify himself with the  salafists the radicals but who  ironically after becoming a grand move t  in 1995 that is the highest religious  authority in chechnya accepted to bless  the jihad against the russian state  siding with the separatist wing led by  the then president jokar dudayev later  the salafists criticized him for being  too lenient which was unacceptable in  their project of real and pure islam as  a result a conflict developed between  sufi and salafist muslims and eventually  ahmad chose to align himself with the  russian leadership and strengthen sufi  rule in chechnya unfortunately for the  kremlin ahmad was not an efficient  puppet he was despised as a corrupt and  cold-hearted politician who argued with  the political partners and civil  administrators that moscow entrusted to  him he preferred to rely on his  relatives and his own security force  known as the zlush babies nasty or  kadyrovzi led by his son ramzan in the  meantime the second chechen war raged  and the chechenization policy didn't  seem to bear fruit as rebel cells  sprouted up all over the country  flooding the media with news of  instability related to the small  caucasian region the climax came in  october 2002 when a commando of rebels  in the service of the insurrectionist  leader shamil basayev besieged the  dubrovka theater in moscow and held more  than 800 people hostage demanding the  withdrawal of russian forces from  chechnya and the end of the conflict the  subsequent raid by the russian special  forces led to the death of about  hostages almost all of them suffocated  by gas shamil named after the famous  warrior imam shamil who led the  resistance of the mountain tribes  against the tsarist armies in the 19th  century claimed the responsibility for  numerous attacks after an incursion into  neighboring dagestan in 1999 he  repeatedly threatened to attack russian  cities even boasting that he had an army  of black widows chetan female kamikaze  his organization planted a bomb in the  moscow subway on the morning of february  6 2004 killing 41 people finally ahmad  the judge the traitor also fell victim  to bazayev's murderous rampage when on  may 9 2004 two days after receiving his  second term as president a bomb exploded  at the stadium in grozny where the  chechen leader and the number of senior  chechen and russian officials were  attending the world war ii victory day  celebration blind to the growing threat  the kremlin continued with its  chationization policy while waiting for  ramzan still too young to reach the  minimum age of 30 years to govern he  designated aloo alkanov as ahmad's  successor however he had no popular base  lacking the charisma and influence that  had distinguished his predecessor  surrounded by many questions about his  real ability to manage a region  devastated by war and to convince the  chechen rebels to lay down their arms  his election took place the weekend  before the event that triggered the  decisive change in putin's approach to  the chechen issue namely the hostage  crisis at the beslan school in north  ossetia on september 1 2004. on that day  more than 330 people lost their lives  many of them children and putin had to  open his eyes to the obvious failure of  his policy four years later in a speech  putin stated that he had underestimated  the complexity and the danger of the  processes taking place in chechnya  failing to react adequately and showing  a weakness it was necessary therefore to  create a new system of forces and means  to exercise control over the situation  in the north caucasus concepts are fully  embodied by the protagonist of our video  ramzan kadyrov he is the master of  chechnya a man who contrary to  expectations has managed to monopolize  power over the chechen security forces  in the territory still it was hard to  expect this from a man who appeared in  audiences before putin dressed in a  training suit and who given his poor  education made every public speech a  shameful disaster in spite of this  kadyrov knew how to operate within the  network of the numerous chechen tapes  the clans and balance power among them  perfectly which explains much of his  strategic success and popularity in the  eyes of his fellow citizens the chechens  are in fact a complex society based on  extended families the tape in fact and  tradition dictates that the omnipotence  of a single tape is unthinkable because  power must be distributed equally among  the various clans according to a  horizontal structure of government this  is precisely the reason that led to the  fall of president ahmad who probably  knew his time was running out when he  affirmed the supremacy of his clan  without consolidating it having to look  more to his hold comrades in arms than  to the neighboring russian giant but  khalif jr didn't repeat his father's  mistakes and enjoying the support of the  kremlin he was able to spend his  resources to concentrate on internal  affairs taking all the risks involved  and eliminating potential rivals the  centralization of power required the  first and foremost to get rid of anyone  who dared to challenge his military  authority especially influential  warlords such as members of the  yamadayev family said magomed kakiev and  mawla di baisarov the yamadayaf brothers  and kahiev commanded the vostok and  zafad battalions respectively each about  900 men strong and the only ethnic  chechens in the russian defense ministry  structure that weren't under chechen  government control zapad formed in 2003  was pro-russian and at the time of the  first chechen war in 1994-1996  opposed the separatist leader dudayev on  the contrary the vastok was formed by  former rebels who passed to the russian  side during the second military campaign  and thanks to their loyalty and  efficiency on the field for the first  time in the modern history of russia  three brothers of the same family the  yamadavs were decorated with medals for  bravery thus enjoying not only the  admiration of moscow for the courage  shown in battle but also the control of  the commercial center of gudermas a city  that lies on the railway junction  between rostov-on-don baku astrakhan and  mazdok there has never been good blood  between the yamadaya family and the  khadirov family and animosity exploded  in april 2008 when fighters of the  vostok battalion engaged in a shootout  with members of ramzan's personal guard  resulting in several deaths in  retaliation the yamadav's older brother  ruslan a former douma deputy was killed  in moscow five months later sulima  commander of the battalion and military  pride of the family managed to escape  from russia and settled in dubai but in  march 2009 adam the lincoln of ramzan's  right hand man had him assassinated  kakiev instead the head of the zapad  battalion then abolished in 2008 was the  only one to survive because he never  questioned ramzan's power finally  mahladi bazarov had been the head of  ahmad's personal security service and  after his death in 2004 he set up the  guardian's security unit on his own  directly reporting to the federal  security service but bizerov was one of  those who liked to play with fire since  he openly criticized ramzan several  times until he released in october 2006  an interview to moscow news in which he  defined him as a medieval tyrant the  reaction of the chechen leader wasn't  long in counting and in fact the  following november baisarov was killed  in moscow by a team of chechen policemen  the goryet's unit disbanded and its  fighters reintegrated in various units  of the chechen ministry of interior once  the main rival forces were defeated the  way was clear for kadyrov he was able to  monopolize the sphere of administration  in the small republic and moscow is not  only uninvolved in church and internal  affairs but receives no information  about the real state of affairs one  could almost say that what happens in  chechnya stays in chechnya and the fact  that the circumstances of natalia  stimirova's murder in 2009 are still  unknown as a concrete proof of that  estemirova a russian activist who worked  with investigative journalists anna  politkovskaya and human rights lawyer  stanislav markelot both of whom murdered  in 2006 and 2009 respectively  documenting hundreds of cases of abuses  in chechnya by government security  forces she carried out her research for  the human rights organization memorial  and was therefore branded as an  undesired person in the eyes of ramzan  who repeatedly stressed his willingness  to silence her forever so that morning  of july 15 2009 when according to the  moscow office of human rights watch  estimirova was kidnapped near her home  in grozny and then found dead in a  wooded area near the village of ghaziart  in ingoshetya there was little doubt as  to who was behind the kidnapping the  problem is that there has never been a  tough stance against ramzan from the  kremlin in fact even though vice  president dmitry medvedev expressed the  indignation and the murder and order to  take all the necessary measures to carry  out the investigation he always rejected  all hypotheses about kalirov's  involvement in the crime  on a  after all there is a dark power packed  between the federal government and small  republic that mustn't be revealed to the  outside world ramzan was charged with  creating the illusion of a peaceful and  flourishing chechnya by any means  necessary which explains his use of  violence outside moscow's control in the  2016 elections ramzan confirmed his role  as the undisputed leader with almost 98  of votes in favor and from that moment  until the present day he has continued  his war against political opponents and  insurgents but why was such a high  degree of consensus reached simple  because in the months leading up to the  vote the authorities undertook fears to  crack down on anyone who thought the  total loyalty to cadillac was  questionable among them were ordinary  people expressing dissent through social  media russian journalists like boris  nyemsov a critic of the chechen  leadership who was assassinated in  moscow on february 2015 and the very few  human rights defenders who dare to  challenge abuses of power by church and  law enforcement and security agencies a  recent report describes contemporary  chechnya as a totalitarian state within  a state characterized by kadyrov's  interference in nearly every aspect of  social life including politics religion  academic discourse and family matters  many experts describe his orders as  being in practice at the only law in the  republic thanks to the cult that has  been created around this figure the main  driving force behind this cult is  grosney tv and state radio whose news  and current affairs programs often  depict kadhirov while also blaming local  high officials for their mistakes it's  well known is intensive use of social  media to set its public agenda identify  and smear enemies think that his  instagram account which he launched in  february 2013 before being banned by  zuckerberg's company had about 1 million  followers in 2015. in more recent times  despite ramzan professing his loyalty to  vladimir putin himself his insistence on  having a free hand in chechnya has  apparently begun to test the kremlin's  patience moscow has condemned albeit in  mild terms some of his more outrageous  actions such as his public efforts to  destroy the homes of alleged rebels and  the numerous fires that followed saying  that no one including kadyrov has the  right to impose extrajudicial punishment  but these are just words and it's  difficult to believe that in the near  future the situation will change also  because moscow needs someone like  kadyrov to keep at bay a territory where  tensions are dormant ready to explode  again well we are done i hope i've kept  your attention up to the end and i'll  see you in the next video ciao

